  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a5787f6180006a664a9f",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cd4ac6696548afc3d12a644dcdcb29df?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cd4ac6696548afc3d12a644dcdcb29df?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cd4ac6696548afc3d12a644dcdcb29df?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cd4ac6696548afc3d12a644dcdcb29df?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMR-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Mark Roy",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a5787f6180006a664a9f",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "A related issue that I just found was a similar behaviour when any datastream is purged from an object the policy is removed from the index and not added back.   ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Another issue that I see from examining the code is when adding any datastream, if the object has a policy it will be added to the index again regardless of whether or not it was already there.   Not sure if the index can handle having two policies for the same object, but I think it is something that should be avoided so that the policies in the index dont become out of sync with the repository.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I will go through the logic of this class and attempt to find some rules that make sense.   I think at least for the datastream modification rules it needs to check if the datastream being operated on is in fact the FESLPOLICY stream.  Otherwise, it makes no sense to change the index.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
